# Heli-VertiSafe — Project Rules for Cursor AI

## PROJECT OVERVIEW
This is a helipad/vertiport feasibility analysis tool. It scores potential helipad zones based on wind, obstacles, terrain, access, geometry, and environment. It generates compliance reports per ICAO and Saudi GACAR standards.

## CRITICAL: DO NOT MODIFY THESE
- **Scoring formulas**: sWind, sObs, sTer, sAcc, sGeo, sEnv — these are calibrated to aviation standards
- **ICAO values**: 1:8 approach gradient, 1:2 transitional, 45m IH, 0.83D TLOF, 95% wind coverage
- **GACAR values**: 2% max slope PC1, 3% PC2/3, 4% SA slope, 30m building clearance, 2D obstacle distance
- **Compliance check clause numbers**: GACAR Part 138.xxx, ICAO Annex 14 Vol II references
- **calcGeom formulas**: FATO = D × fatoMin, SA = max(D×0.25, 3), etc.
- **calcOrientation logic**: crosswind/headwind decomposition, 5° heading increment scan
- **autoCalcCoords**: bidirectional X,Y ↔ Distance,Bearing conversion. Both directions must always work.
- **Aircraft data**: D-values, MTOW, crosswind limits — these are from manufacturer specs

## AVIATION TERMINOLOGY
- FATO = Final Approach and Take-Off area
- SA = Safety Area (surrounds FATO)
- TLOF = Touchdown and Lift-Off area
- OLS = Obstacle Limitation Surface
- D-value = Reference dimension of largest helicopter (overall length including rotors)
- PC1/PC2/PC3 = Performance Class (determines slope limits and approach requirements)
- GACAR = General Authority of Civil Aviation Regulation (Saudi Arabia)
- ICAO = International Civil Aviation Organization
- AGL = Above Ground Level
- AMSL = Above Mean Sea Level
- NOTAM = Notice to Airmen

## DATA MODEL
- Project (proj): contains helicopter selection, PC, mode, weights, workflow, audit log
- Site: lat/lng/elev, study area dimensions, grid size, exclusions, boundary, destinations
- Zone: corners (polygon), wind data, obstacles array, terrain, access, sensitivity, vertiport, source tags, scores
- Obstacle: name, type, height AGL, width, length, x, y, distance, bearing, corners (polygon), confidence
- Sensitivity Zone: name, type, level (low/medium/high), distance, bearing, x, y
- Access Node: name, type, distance, bearing, x, y, importance (1-5)

## REDUCER ACTIONS (30+)
STEP, TAB, UP, US, SZ, SEL, ZF, AO, UO, DO, TOG, ASENS, USENS, DSENS, ANODE, UNODE, DNODE, AEXCL, UEXCL, DEXCL, ADEST, UDEST, DDEST, RUN, SAVE_SCENARIO, DEL_SCENARIO, DUP_SCENARIO, LOAD_SCENARIO, WHATIF, WORKFLOW, IMPORT, DEMO, RESET, APPLY_ALL, UNDO, REDO

## CODING STANDARDS
- Use functional React components with hooks (no class components except ErrorBoundary)
- Keep the dark theme: bg=#050a12, surface=#0b1120, text=#e1e7ef, cyan=#06b6d4, green=#10b981
- Font: Outfit (Google Fonts)
- All measurements in meters unless stated otherwise
- Wind speed in knots
- Angles in degrees (convert to radians with DEG = Math.PI/180)
- Always maintain bidirectional auto-calc: when X or Y changes → recalc Distance + Bearing, and vice versa

## WHEN ADDING NEW FEATURES
1. Never break existing scoring/compliance logic
2. New UI components should follow the existing glassmorphism style (hvs-card, hvs-glass classes)
3. New data fields should be added to the appropriate mk* factory function with defaults
4. New reducer actions should follow the pattern: return { ...state, [updated field], scored: false }
5. Always handle null/undefined gracefully — the app should never crash on missing data

## TESTING CHECKLIST
After any change, verify:
- [ ] Welcome screen loads
- [ ] Demo data loads correctly
- [ ] All 6 steps render without errors
- [ ] Run Analysis produces scores
- [ ] Compliance checks show PASS/FAIL
- [ ] 3D view renders (Three.js)
- [ ] File import works (at least CSV)
- [ ] Export/Import JSON works
- [ ] Undo/Redo works (Ctrl+Z/Y)
- [ ] No console errors

## FILE STRUCTURE (after split)
```
src/
├── App.jsx              # Main shell
├── components/
│   ├── WelcomeScreen.jsx
│   ├── steps/           # 6 step views
│   ├── charts/          # SVG + Three.js
│   ├── ui/              # Tag, ScoreBar, ZGrid, etc.
│   └── report/          # Report + PDF
├── engine/              # Scoring + compliance (PURE FUNCTIONS — do not add UI here)
├── parsers/             # File format parsers
├── data/                # Constants + models + demo
├── state/               # Reducer + undo + autosave
├── utils/               # Theme + coords + geometry
└── types/               # TypeScript interfaces (after TS migration)
```
